\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Signs under a change of operator}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Each self-opposite block is a finite spectral problem. The [inversion product](fdip-01AV) records inversion signs of its negative pairs. The paired Pfaffian factors in \ref{fdip-01AT} also depend on real volumes and the signs of Hermitian summands. Which signs persist along a specified class of deformations, and which symmetry hypotheses would put the whole family in a fixed class? A classification requires both the allowed families and a rule for comparing their members.}
